---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy - Kasra Dash';
const description =
  'How kasradash.com collects, uses and protects your personal data — covering the contact and lead forms, newsletter, embedded videos and hosting analytics.';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/privacy-policy/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} path="/privacy-policy/" breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <main>
    <section class="border-b border-tint-border bg-tint">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
        <Breadcrumbs {crumbs} />
        <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
          How this website collects, uses and protects your personal data.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
      <p class="mb-10 max-w-3xl rounded-[20px] border border-amber-400/40 bg-amber-400/10 px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold text-amber-200">
        Draft — review before launch. This policy was prepared for review and has not yet been
        approved. Confirm the details below (controller name, retention periods, analytics tooling)
        before publishing the site.
      </p>

      <div class="prose prose-kasra max-w-3xl">
        <p><em>Last updated: 11 August 2026</em></p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          This website, kasradash.com (the "site"), is operated by Kasra Dash ("we", "us"), an
          entrepreneur and SEO consultant based in Manchester, UK. For the purposes of UK data
          protection law (the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018), Kasra Dash is the data
          controller for personal data collected through this site. You can contact us about
          anything in this policy at <a href="mailto:me@kasradash.com">me@kasradash.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect and why</h2>

        <h3>Contact and lead forms</h3>
        <p>
          The form on our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> is provided by HighLevel Inc.
          ("GoHighLevel", served from api.leadconnectorhq.com) and is embedded on this site. When
          you submit the form we collect the details you enter — typically your name, email address,
          phone number and information about your business or enquiry. We use this information to
          respond to your enquiry, provide what you requested and, where you have agreed, to send
          you relevant follow-up messages. GoHighLevel processes this data on our behalf.
        </p>

        <h3>Newsletter</h3>
        <p>
          The site no longer hosts a newsletter signup; community membership runs through The New
          Search on Skool (skool.com), which has its own privacy policy. If you previously joined
          the mailing list we hold your email address under your consent, and you can withdraw it
          at any time using the unsubscribe link in any email or by contacting us. We do not sell
          your email address or share it with third parties for their own marketing.
        </p>

        <h3>Embedded videos</h3>
        <p>
          Some pages embed videos hosted on YouTube. When you view or play an embedded video,
          YouTube (Google) may set cookies and collect data about your viewing, your device and, if
          you are signed in, your Google account, under{' '}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.
          We do not control this processing.
        </p>

        <h3>Hosting and analytics</h3>
        <p>
          Our hosting provider automatically records standard server logs — including IP addresses,
          browser type and pages requested — to deliver the site, keep it secure and produce
          aggregate traffic statistics. This information is not used to identify individual
          visitors.
        </p>

        <h2>Our lawful bases</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Consent</strong> — the newsletter and any optional marketing follow-up.</li>
          <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — responding to enquiries, keeping the site secure and understanding aggregate site usage.</li>
          <li><strong>Contract</strong> — where you engage us for consulting or related services.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
        <p>
          We share personal data only with the service providers that run this site and our
          business: HighLevel Inc. (forms, lead management and email), Google (embedded YouTube
          videos) and our hosting provider. Each acts under its own terms and, where it processes
          data for us, under a data processing agreement. We do not sell personal data.
        </p>

        <h2>International transfers</h2>
        <p>
          Some of these providers (including HighLevel Inc. and Google) store data outside the UK,
          including in the United States. Where that happens, transfers are protected by
          safeguards recognised under UK law, such as the UK Extension to the EU–US Data Privacy
          Framework or the International Data Transfer Agreement / standard contractual clauses.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep your data</h2>
        <p>
          We keep enquiry and lead data for as long as needed to handle your enquiry and any
          resulting business relationship, and newsletter data until you unsubscribe. Server logs
          are retained for short periods by our hosting provider. We delete or anonymise data when
          it is no longer needed.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under the UK GDPR you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
          <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
          <li>have your data erased;</li>
          <li>restrict or object to our processing of it;</li>
          <li>receive a portable copy of data you provided to us;</li>
          <li>withdraw consent at any time, where consent is our lawful basis.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, email{' '}
          <a href="mailto:me@kasradash.com">me@kasradash.com</a>. You also have the right to
          complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at{' '}
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site does not set cookies of its own. Embedded third-party content — the GoHighLevel
          forms and YouTube videos described above — may set cookies when you interact with it. You
          can block or delete cookies through your browser settings; doing so may stop the embedded
          forms or videos from working.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top shows
          when it last changed, and significant changes will be highlighted on this page.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy or your data: <a href="mailto:me@kasradash.com">me@kasradash.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
